cluster-judge.instruction:
Read docs/TASK_PHASE7.md FIRST -- sections 2.2 and 3.2, which is your acceptance -- and the four examples of Function Recheck Watchlist in the cluster group of contour.yaml. ethsc/cluster.py is in your context: read it, do not modify it. You patch only tests/test_cluster_examples.py. Keep all eight existing tests exactly as they are.

Add one test per new contour example, four in all:
(a) the store from codes_26077729.json with the seed 0xb4e16d0168e52d35cacd2c6185b44281ec28c9dc labelled "UniV2 pair seed" gives exactly 4 alerts -- 0x22052a1a..., 0x2621cc0b... and 0x3041cbd3... with 1.0, then 0xcf6daab9... with 26/32 -- and the seed's own address is not among them;
(b) the same store with min_score=1.0 gives only the three 1.0 alerts, and with seed_addresses=[the seed address in UPPER case] gives the same list as the default call;
(c) a store holding code_belle.hex at 0x34c6211621f2763c60eb007dc2ae91090a2d22f6 and its four code_belle_copy_*.hex at 0x1807090dd15a6f58e00fd769e32ebf20ee610385, 0x2141be5f2afa674c94167ab167a478a56cb539f5, 0x46cadea509dc3d3c96a11fb61ab8b222f5238f0a and 0x6411bed82614b91ef655d82486e0bd3a13d2eb8c, seeded "BELLE honeypot", gives the same 4 alerts twice in a row, each score 13/15, in that address order;
(d) that store with no seeds gives [], and with seed_addresses=["0x1111111111111111111111111111111111111111"] gives [] as well.

Your tests are the judge, so they compare the exact list, not a length: a mutation check runs them against a recheck_watchlist that keeps the seed's own address and sorts by score only, and at least two of your tests must go red on it. Set maxDiff = None on your class so a failing comparison prints the difference.

Use the loaders already in the file (_block_store, _read_hex, _temp_db) and do NOT import tests.helpers -- the acceptance rejects it. Every assert needs msg=. Do not touch any other file.

rpc-judge.acceptance:
D=/tmp/morph/rpc-judge; mkdir -p $D; S=$(date +%s)-$$; L=$D/acc-$S.log
cp tests/test_rpc_examples.py $D/0-$S.py 2>/dev/null
K=$(sed -n 's/^[[:space:]]*INFURA_API_KEY[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*//p' .env 2>/dev/null | tr -d "\"' \r" | head -n 1)
export INFURA_API_KEY=TESTKEY-ENV-0000
pyt() { venv/bin/python -c "import socket, sys, pytest
def _blocked(*a, **k):
    raise OSError('network blocked')
socket.getaddrinfo = _blocked; socket.socket.connect = _blocked; socket.create_connection = _blocked
sys.exit(pytest.main(sys.argv[1:]))" "$@"; }
(
 set -e
 venv/bin/python -c "import ast,sys; [ast.parse(open(f).read(), f, feature_version=(3,9)) for f in sys.argv[1:]]" tests/test_rpc_examples.py
 venv/bin/python - rpc-judge <<'PY'
import ast, glob, sys
card = sys.argv[1]
NET = ("urllib", "http", "socket")
def imports(path):
    """Every imported module of a file, from the AST, never from its text."""
    out = []
    for n in ast.walk(ast.parse(open(path, encoding="utf-8").read(), path)):
        if isinstance(n, ast.Import):
            out += [a.name for a in n.names]
        elif isinstance(n, ast.ImportFrom):
            base = "." * n.level + (n.module or "")
            out.append(base)
            out += [base.rstrip(".") + "." + a.name if base.strip(".") else base + a.name for a in n.names]
    return out
def top(m):
    return m.lstrip(".").split(".")[0]
bad = []
for p in sorted(glob.glob("ethsc/*.py")):
    if p != "ethsc/rpc.py":
        bad += ["No Network In Core: %s imports %s; only ethsc/rpc.py may" % (p, m) for m in imports(p) if top(m) in NET]
if card == "rpc":
    if imports("ethsc/config.py"):
        bad.append("ethsc/config.py must hold data only, no imports: %s" % imports("ethsc/config.py"))
    mods = imports("ethsc/rpc.py")
    allowed = set(sys.stdlib_module_names) | {"ethsc", "config", "__future__"}
    bad += ["ethsc/rpc.py imports %s: standard library and ethsc.config only" % m for m in mods if top(m) not in allowed or (top(m) == "ethsc" and m != "ethsc" and not m.startswith("ethsc.config"))]
    if not any(top(m) == "urllib" for m in mods):
        bad.append("ethsc/rpc.py must import urllib for its default transport")
    tests = ["tests/test_rpc.py"]
elif card == "ingest":
    for m in imports("ethsc/ingest.py"):
        if top(m) in NET + ("sqlite3",) or m.lstrip(".") in ("ethsc.rpc", "ethsc.config", "rpc", "config") or m in (".rpc", ".config"):
            bad.append("ethsc/ingest.py imports %s: no network, no sqlite3, no ethsc.rpc or ethsc.config (rpc and prices are parameters)" % m)
    for n in ast.walk(ast.parse(open("ethsc/ingest.py", encoding="utf-8").read())):
        if isinstance(n, ast.Attribute) and n.attr == "_conn":
            bad.append("ethsc/ingest.py line %d reads a private Store attribute; use the public Store API" % n.lineno)
    tests = ["tests/test_ingest.py"]
else:
    tests = ["tests/test_%s_examples.py" % card.replace("-judge", "")]
for t in tests:
    bad += ["%s imports %s: tests stay offline" % (t, m) for m in imports(t) if top(m) in NET]
print("\n".join("guard: " + b for b in bad) if bad else "guard: ast imports OK")
sys.exit(1 if bad else 0)
PY
 pyt tests/test_rpc_examples.py -q --tb=short
 pyt tests -q --tb=short
) > $L 2>&1; rc=$?
if [ -n "$K" ] && grep -qF -- "$K" $L ethsc/*.py tests/*.py; then echo 'guard: Secret Hygiene: the real Infura key shows in the output or the code'; rc=1; fi
if [ -n "$K" ]; then sed "s|$K|<KEY>|g" $L; else cat $L; fi; exit $rc
